{"name":"Lychee","hex":"#cd0c41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lychee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The Chinese tropical fruit tree Litchi chinensis, of the soapberry family.","That tree's bright red oval fruit with a single stone surrounded by a fleshy white aril."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lychee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lychee","blocks":[{"text":"Lychees are the fruit of the tree Litchi chinensis, the sole member of the genus Litchi, part of the soapberry family, Sapindaceae. They are edible, with a sweet, mildly tart flavor, and have a distinctive floral aroma often described as rose-like."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Litchi_chinensis_fruits.JPG/330px-Litchi_chinensis_fruits.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lychee","wikidata":"Q13182"},{"title":"Lychee (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Lychee is the third extended play by New Zealand singer-songwriter Benee released on 4 March 2022 through Republic Records. Consisting of seven tracks and a duration of around twenty-five minutes, it was primarily produced by Josh Fountain, who was accompanied by Greg Kurstin, Kenny Beats, and Rostam. The album centers on emotional turmoil, relationships, and personal growth. For its concept and title, Bennett was having trouble choosing an adequate title, so she had decided to go with a name of something she loved."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/Lychee_by_Benee.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lychee_(EP)","wikidata":"Q130265220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Sonnerat_litchi.jpg/330px-Sonnerat_litchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Sonnerat_litchi.jpg/330px-Sonnerat_litchi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pierre Sonnerat's drawing from Voyage aux Indes Orientales et à la Chine (1782)[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASonnerat_litchi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/1280px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg/500px-Lychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whole and opened fruit with seed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALychee_fruits_and_seed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Flora_Sinensis_1656_%282950635%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Lici Fruit Tree\" in Michał Boym's Flora Sinensis (1657)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlora_Sinensis_1656_(2950635)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Litchi_root.jpg/500px-Litchi_root.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or